{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-78549-r4615199","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Pigeon Pea and Fenugreek Curry (Methi Tadka Dal)","sourcePageId":78549,"sourceRevision":"4615199","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-03T02:37:38Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Pigeon%20Pea%20and%20Fenugreek%20Curry%20(Methi%20Tadka%20Dal)&oldid=4615199","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:20:18.668Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Indian recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for curry","Category:Recipes for dal","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using chickpea","Category:Recipes using coriander","Category:Recipes using curry leaf","Category:Recipes using fenugreek leaf","Category:Recipes using fresh ginger","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using lentil","Category:Recipes using mustard seed","Category:Recipes with images"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"bc863e943d472ba8896a9213241327d69d73ae515f849d2085f15c638c69109c","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary\n| category = Side dish recipes\n| servings = 4–6\n| time = 12–15 minutes\n| difficulty = 2\n| Image = [[File:Dal Tadka.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|Cuisine of India]]\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Pigeon Pea|toor]] [[Cookbook:Dal|dal]]\n* 2 cups [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n* 2 handfuls of [[Cookbook:Fenugreek|methi leaves]] (only the leaves without the tender stem)\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]]\n* 1 big [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] of [[Cookbook:Turmeric|turmeric powder]]\n* 1–2 [[Cookbook:Chili Pepper|green chillis]], [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]]\n* 10 whole [[Cookbook:Pepper|black peppercorns]]\n* 1 small dollop of [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n* 1 small piece of [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]] (optional)\n* 2 spoonfuls [[Cookbook:Ghee|ghee]]\n* ½ small spoon of [[Cookbook:Mustard|mustard seeds]]\n* ½ small spoon of [[Cookbook:Cumin|zheera (cumin)]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic cloves]], sliced\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Chili Pepper|red chillis]]\n* 6–8 [[Cookbook:Curry Leaf|curry leaves]]\n* 1 small tomato, finely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* [[Cookbook:Chili Powder|Chilli powder]]\n* Ground [[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander]]\n* [[Cookbook:Lemon Juice|Lemon juice]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Mix all above and put them in an Indian cooker ([[Cookbook:Pressure Cooking|pressure cooker]]). Wait until the dal is cooked (4 whistles).\n# Heat the ghee in a pan, and add the mustard seeds, zheera, garlic, red chillis, and curry leaves. [[Cookbook:Frying|Fry]] until the garlic is golden.\n# Add the chopped tomato, salt, chilli powder, and coriander to taste.\n# Add the cooked dal mixture to the fried mixture, and let it [[Cookbook:Simmering|simmer]]. You can add water if you like it to be more like gravy.\n# Add two drops of lemon juice for added taste.\n# Serve with hot rice, and an optional touch of Gongura pickle.\n\n==See also==\n*[[Cookbook:Tadka dhal|Tadka dhal]]\n*[[Cookbook:Tadkal|Tadkal]]\n\n[[Category:Recipes using chickpea]]\n[[Category:Recipes for curry]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lentil]]\n[[Category:Indian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coriander]]\n[[Category:Recipes using curry leaf]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dal]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fenugreek leaf]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard seed]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Pigeon Pea and Fenugreek Curry (Methi Tadka Dal)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"4–6","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"½ cup toor dal","sourceText":"½ cup toor dal","amountText":"½ cup toor dal","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 cups water","sourceText":"2 cups water","amountText":"2 cups water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 handfuls of methi leaves (only the leaves without the tender stem)","sourceText":"2 handfuls of methi leaves (only the leaves without the tender stem)","amountText":"2 handfuls of methi leaves (only the leaves without the tender stem)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"3 tomatoes","sourceText":"3 tomatoes","amountText":"3 tomatoes","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 big onion","sourceText":"1 big onion","amountText":"1 big onion","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 pinch of turmeric powder","sourceText":"1 pinch of turmeric powder","amountText":"1 pinch of turmeric powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1–2 green chillis, sliced","sourceText":"1–2 green chillis, sliced","amountText":"1–2 green chillis, sliced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"10 whole black peppercorns","sourceText":"10 whole black peppercorns","amountText":"10 whole black peppercorns","amount":null,"unit":null,"fo